{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210732,"nonce":"L4Bjz2IluFRRBSq5jrW4jUhQDWw=","title":"hatch bundles: relative-path imports not normalised in reachability + var resolution","message":"Fixed in commit 78f0234. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n`@hatch:web` (and any bundled package with sibling modules) failed at runtime under interpreter mode: `App.new()` raised `Null does not implement 'new()'` at `Stylesheet.new()`, because the `Stylesheet` slot in `@hatch:web`'s module_vars was `null`.\n\n**Root cause (two sites, both missed):**\n\n1. `compute_reachable_hatch_modules` (`vm.rs:4958+`) walked imports from `entry` to compute which sections to install. Sibling-module imports like `import \"./css\" for Css, Style, Stylesheet` were looked up in the section table verbatim — but sections were keyed `\"css\"` (bare). The miss dropped `css`, `forms`, `live` from `install_order` entirely, and `@hatch:web` ran with null var slots for all 10 of their exports.\n\n2. The runtime var-resolution fallback at `install_module_mir_and_run_with_sources` already stripped `./` / `../` / replaced `/` with `.`, but the file resolver (`main.rs:make_module_io`) appends `.wren` via `with_wren_suffix` whenever a relative candidate path doesn't exist on disk (which is always the case for bundled siblings). So `canonical = \"./css.wren\"`, stripped = `\"css.wren\"`, and `find_imported_var_from(\"Stylesheet\", \"css.wren\")` missed the `\"css\"` module.\n\n**Why:** the symptom only surfaced when a `wlift` instance was running with a filesystem resolver active (the `main.wren` case) AND the imported module came from a bundled artifact rather than a path-link. Path-linked deps don't hit this code path; bundle-only deps without sibling modules don't hit it either. `@hatch:web` is the first bundle with siblings to ship.\n\n**How to apply:** both fix sites now strip `./`/`../`/`.wren` and rewrite `/` → `.` before looking up the bundle's bare name. Future packages that follow the same path-relative pattern Just Work.\n\nFixed in commit 78f0234 (2026-05-11). Verified the site boot moves past `App.new` and reaches `Catalog.boot()`; the actual remaining hang is unrelated (`@hatch:sqlite` cache ABI; see `project_sqlite_cached_hang.md`).","files":null}]}